# M1 / B018 — modern-csharp, persistence-change, project-structure references (backend-layout, solution-layout).

C R191 OL PST-010 | MUST | Treat EF Core migrations as source code: review every generated migration before committing it (destructive schema changes, unexpected column recreation, data migrations, indexes, foreign keys, delete behavior); do not casually alter existing migrations, and regenerate or edit an uncommitted migration only when that matches the project's migration workflow. | EF Core migrations | Editing an uncommitted migration per the project workflow.
C R192 OL PST-008 | MUST | Whenever Domain or persistence changes affect seeded entities, update the development DbSeeder in the same change (new required or removed/renamed properties, changed relationships, new required related entities, changed enum/status values, new entity states, changed invariants) and review it together with the corresponding migration; recreating the Development database at any revision yields valid representative seed data. | seed data co-change | Already seeded rows of an existing database are not patched.
C R193 OL DEP-022 | DEFAULT | Use the .slnx solution format (with the .sln exception stated in the technology stack). | solution file | .sln exception in the technology stack.
C R194 OL DEP-023 | DEFAULT | Directory.Build.props holds shared .NET settings (TargetFramework, Nullable, ImplicitUsings, analysis/compiler settings) and no genuinely project-specific settings; properties duplicated by dotnet new in project files are removed. | shared .NET build configuration | none stated
C R195 OL WF-005 | MUST | Build the affected projects and run the relevant tests for the change; for persistence changes run the persistence and integration tests and confirm the migration applies to a freshly created Development database before seeding. | verification | none stated
C X29 EX DEP-008,DEP-003 | MUST | global.json pins the intended stable SDK line; when scaffolding select the current stable SDK for the target .NET release (no RC/preview SDK unless explicitly requested) and allow servicing through the chosen rollForward policy. | repository SDK configuration | Preview SDK explicitly requested. | DEP-008 fixes the .NET platform and DEP-003 package versions; no oracle policy requires an SDK pin file. | A repository without global.json does not follow the instruction.

